  "about": "Names of places outside India and of other cultures, by which a live-research write-back is told to be about somewhere other than an Indian craft (decision 0135). Countries are the member and observer states of the United Nations, with Taiwan and Kosovo, other than India, under their English short names and the adjectives English uses for them. Regions and cultures are those that craft, ceramics, textile and metal literature names. Left out on purpose: English (a language of India), Mali (a gardeners' community), Tonga (a carriage), Bali (an earring), Holland (a linen), Wales (the ribs of a fabric), Polish (a finish), Arabic (a script of Indian calligraphy), Tibet (Tibetan carpets are an Indian craft), Sindh (Sindhi communities practise in India), Asia and South Asia (India is in them) and Roman (a typeface and its numerals). Other senses are the names a place word takes inside a material, colour, knot or finish (china clay, Turkey red, German silver) or a sea that washes India (the Arabian Sea); a place word inside one of them names no place abroad. Also left out: Maya (an Indian name and idea). Kept by hand: a write-back refused for a word used in another sense is a reason to add another sense or leave the name out, with a line in the decision log.",
